Z||000002||pontiacs4me||07-07-2001||02:32 AM||||Ive had flushmount front signal lights on my car forever, but nobody cares about them.  Ive posted pics a million times but nobody wants to know anything about them, or how I made them or how I mounted them.  <BR>Ok heres the pic.  Again.<BR> <A HREF="http://home.kscable.com/ccheney/ryanpict/fiero9.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://home.kscable.com/ccheney/ryanpict/fiero9.jpg</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Urchin||07-07-2001||11:39 AM||||hey!   pontiacs4me:   Sorry I've missed previous posts I guess, but I'd be interested in how you did that.  I had thought about doing that before but could not come up with a practical idea of fastening them.  Any info would be appreciated.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lowered_blackgtsig2a_2.jpg"> <BR>If you can read this, I'm parked.||||reg||1
Z||000004||pontiacs4me||07-07-2001||06:19 PM||||Urchin,<BR>I used the housings from a 3rd gen camaro, I cut the amber lens off the housing, then had to cut the top of the housing back about a half an inch.  I sanded the flange smooth, and had to sand it to fit inside the hole.  I used lexan to make the new lense.  I cut it to fit perfectly, and used lexan glue to attach it.  As for bracketry, on the back of the camaro housing, there are 2 bolts that attach to the radiator core support of the camaro, I used that metal strapping that has holes in it like every 3/4 of an inch, and bolted a piece about 6 inches long to the inside hole.  Then reaching around the inside of the radiator opening in the fascia I bent it around to hold it in on the inside.  On the other hole I took a piece of strapping about 12 inches long, and fed it through the hole in the core support, where the wiring goes through, I took the headlight buckets out and took a self tapping screw and screwed down the strapping to the sheet metal under the headlight.  <BR>now there is this stuff called night shades, I used that to black it out, because I decided to go with the black and white theme with my car.  Thats about it really, about the best advice you can get when making these, is just use trial and error, and do whatever you can to make them fit.  Good luck.||||reg||1
